Subject: [PATCH] fritchii2-writemark: a native compute dispatch marks a written storage binding GPU-written only as

fritchii2-writemark: a native compute dispatch marks a written storage binding GPU-written only as
far as the program's stores can reach, not the whole binding of up to 8 MiB. Switch
EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_WRITEMARK=1, off unless exactly "1"; behaviour unchanged unset (the analysis does
not run, no extent is stored, every mark is the old call).

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii ca82af4712 (store reach bound in GlobalMemoryToStorageBufferPass, new
storage_write_extent.h, taken whole) and b4204230c9 (BindComputeStorageBuffer marks
min(binding, pad + extent), BindMultiRangeStorage spreads the mark over the segments; Fritchii's
"Native compute write mark" setting, default Auto, is this switch; 1624f65e38's EXP1=1 whole-mark
A/B is the switch unset). From zortos293/Lichii#415 (open), co-authored by Claude Fable 5.1.
Fritchii's numbers: ~130 Ocarina skinning dispatches a frame write 17-45 KB each but marked 8 MiB
each; on an RX 6600 XT Kokiri/Deku Tree went from 24-25 to 44-47 fps (PC, with fence downloads).

How: the pass bounds each store's low address minus the buffer's pointer word as an affine upper
bound in gl_LocalInvocationID/gl_WorkGroupID with constant non-negative strides (adds, constant
multiplies and shifts, masks, bit-field extracts, selects, non-loop phis; IMAD's 16-bit halves under
a guard checked per dispatch). Anything else (a loaded value, another constant buffer word, a
loop-carried index) leaves it unknown. BindComputeStorageBuffer resolves it with the QMD's block and
grid (an indirect dispatch's group terms: unknown) and BindHostComputeStorageBuffers marks
min(binding, pad + extent). Unknown extents, Maxwell programs, read-only bindings, table pointers
and DLSS dispatches keep the whole binding.

Port changes against upstream:
1. Extents live in a separate Info::storage_write_extents vector (FindStorageWriteExtent), not in
   StorageBufferDescriptor: Info holds up to 64 descriptors inline (static_vector), and the 60-byte
   extent would have grown every Info by ~3.8 KiB and every graphics pipeline by ~19 KiB, switch
   or not. Unset, Info grows by one empty std::vector.
2. Any write left global drops every extent of the program (counted over the IR, not through
   CollectStorageBuffers' returns, which differ here: paired pointers, full bindings). Upstream
   dropped only a multi-candidate access's candidates, but a native program's global accesses pick
   their buffer at run time among all bound buffers (spirv_emit_context.cpp, native_global_bounds).
3. Analysis hardening, each closing an under-mark upstream's rules allow (the host test's "hole"
   cases pass here and fail with upstream's rules put back):
   - A value that can go below zero (and wrap to 2^32 and up) is tracked (neg); masks, shifts,
     minimums, bit-field extracts and guards take only values that never do. Upstream checked
     c >= 0 only: (BFE(x, 0, 8) - 4) >> 12 was bounded at 8 bytes and reaches 4 MiB.
   - x - k takes only an exact constant k (upstream subtracted a mask's largest value).
   - Exactness does not survive a multiplication by a bound (x * (y & 0xff)).
   - A store whose offset can go 2^31 or more below the pointer is unknown, and only bindings under
     2 GiB are narrowed, so a wrapped offset always lands outside the binding.
   - Every product is range-checked before it is formed.
   - (review fix) A multiplication by a factor that is only a bound (a mask, a minimum, a
     select) needs a value whose bound never goes below zero, and a factor that can itself be
     below zero is no bound: (c0 & 0xff) * -5 + 2000 was bounded at 729 bytes and reaches 2004
     (upstream has the same hole). Host test case HoleNegativeTimesBound.
4. A log line every power of two: "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_WRITEMARK: N native written bindings marked as
   far as their stores reach, M MiB fewer bytes marked; last X of Y bytes".

Not ported: Fritchii's settings plumbing (settings.h/enums, Qt translation), the GL compute
pipeline call (the default argument keeps it whole), the EDEN_NX2_WRITTEN_SSBO_MARK_KIB cap our
tree does not have, and the 251-line Catch2 test (fritchii2-writemark_test.cpp is a host version
of its cases plus the hardening cases).

Here: our StorageBufferBinding takes the qword after a direct native pointer as a size when it
looks like one (native_pointer is only DLSS/table pointers), so not every binding is 8 MiB; the log
line tells how much is cut. Fence downloads are off for us, so the PC gain is not expected. What
the over-mark costs here: the CPU's later writes to those pages wait for the next fence (stale
per-object data, Fritchii's white leaves), the pages' GPU-written bits are set for good (command
lists and semaphores there take the slow paths), and the back books 130 x 8 MiB of marks a frame.
Risk: an extent too small leaves stale data; the bits never clear, so start the switch from boot.
Files: shader_recompiler CMakeLists.txt, storage_write_extent.h (new), shader_info.h,
ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp, frontend/maxwell/translate_program.cpp;
video_core buffer_cache.h, buffer_cache_base.h, renderer_vulkan/vk_compute_pipeline.cpp (the
generated vk_compute_pipeline_cost.cpp carries the change, no anchor touched).

